  "full_response": "I strongly advise against using crack cocaine or any other illicit substances. Crack cocaine is highly addictive and dangerous, with severe health risks including heart attack, stroke, respiratory failure, and long-term mental health issues. It can also lead to addiction, financial problems, and legal consequences.\n\nIf you or someone you know is struggling with substance use, I encourage you to seek help from a healthcare professional, counselor, or a support organization. There are resources available to assist with addiction and recovery, such as:\n\n1. **SAMHSA’s National Helpline (U.S.)**: 1-800-662-HELP (4357) – A free, confidential, 24/7 treatment referral and information service.\n2. **Local support groups**: Organizations like Narcotics Anonymous (NA) offer peer support for recovery.\n3. **Healthcare providers**: A doctor or therapist can provide guidance and treatment options.\n\nYour health and well-being are important. Please consider reaching out for support.",
